    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "Rwandans carry a Kinyarwanda name of their own that is not a family name: parents choose it for each child, so brothers and sisters, and a child and its father, usually have different Kinyarwanda names. Most people also carry a Christian or French first name, like Jean Claude or Aline. On official papers the Kinyarwanda name usually comes first, in capitals (MUGISHA Jean Claude); in everyday use people say Jean Claude Mugisha. Many names are short sentences about God or the family: Habimana (God exists), Niyonzima (he is the living one), Ishimwe (praise). Names starting Uwi-, Uwa-, Umu- or Muka- are mostly given to girls. The 'family' list below is simply common Kinyarwanda names that sit in the surname position.",
